## iti69
iti69:1.1 | S: This was said by the Buddha, the Perfected One: that is what I heard. | T: This was said by the Blessed One, said by the Arahant, so I have heard:
iti69:2.1 | S: “Whoever has not given up greed, hate, and delusion | T: “Monks, anyone–monk or nun–in whom passion is unabandoned, aversion is unabandoned, & delusion is unabandoned,
iti69:2.2 | S: is said to have not crossed over the ocean with its waves and whirlpools, its saltwater crocodiles and monsters. | T: is said not to have crossed the ocean with its waves, breakers, & whirlpools, its seizers & demons.
iti69:2.3 | S: Whoever has given up greed, hate, and delusion | T: Anyone–monk or nun–in whom passion is abandoned, aversion is abandoned, & delusion is abandoned,
iti69:2.4 | S: is said to have crossed over the ocean with its waves and whirlpools, its saltwater crocodiles and monsters. Crossed over and gone to the far shore, that brahmin stands on solid ground.” | T: is said to have crossed the ocean with its waves, breakers, & whirlpools, its seizers & demons. Having crossed over, having reached the far shore, he/she stands on high ground, a brahman.”
iti69:2.5 | S: The Buddha spoke this matter. | T: (none)
iti69:2.6 | S: On this it is said: | T: (none)
iti69:3.1 | S: “Those in whom greed, hate, and ignorance | T: One whose passion, aversion, & ignorance
iti69:3.2 | S: have faded away, | T: have faded away,
iti69:3.3 | S: have crossed the ocean so hard to cross, | T: has crossed over this ocean
iti69:3.4 | S: with its saltwater crocodiles and monsters, <j>its waves and dangers. | T: with its seizers, demons, dangerous waves, so hard to cross.
iti69:4.1 | S: They’ve slipped their chains, given up death, and have no attachments. | T: Free from acquisitions –bonds surmounted, death abandoned–
iti69:4.2 | S: They’ve given up suffering, <j>so there are no more future lives. | T: he has abandoned stress with no further becoming.
iti69:4.3 | S: They’ve disappeared and cannot be defined; | T: Having gone to the goal he is undefined,
iti69:4.4 | S: they’ve confounded the King of Death, I say.” | T: has outwitted, I tell you, the King of Death.
iti69:5.1 | S: This too is a matter that was spoken by the Blessed One: that is what I heard. | T: (none)
iti69:5.2 | P: Dasamaṁ. | T: (none)
iti69:5.3 | P: Dutiyo vaggo. | T: (none)
iti69:6.0 | P: Tassuddānaṁ | T: (none)
iti69:6.1 | P: Puññaṁ cakkhu atha indriyāni, | T: (none)
iti69:6.2 | P: Addhā ca caritaṁ duve soci; | T: (none)
iti69:6.3 | P: Muno atha rāgaduve, | T: (none)
iti69:6.4 | P: Puna vaggamāhu dutiyamuttamanti. | T: (none)

## iti70
iti70:1.1 | S: This was said by the Buddha, the Perfected One: that is what I heard. | T: This was said by the Blessed One, said by the Arahant, so I have heard:
iti70:2.1 | S: “Mendicants, I’ve seen beings who engaged in misconduct by body, speech, and mind, who denounced the noble ones, who had wrong views and acted accordingly. | T: “Monks, I have seen beings who–endowed with bodily misconduct, verbal misconduct, & mental misconduct; who reviled noble ones, held wrong views and undertook actions under the influence of wrong views–
iti70:2.2 | S: At the breaking up of the body, after death, they were reborn in a place of loss, a bad place, the underworld, hell. | T: at the break-up of the body, after death, have re-appeared in the plane of deprivation, the bad destination, the lower realms, in hell.
iti70:3.1 | S: Now, I don’t say this because I’ve heard it from some other ascetic or brahmin. | T: It is not from having heard this from another contemplative or brahman that I tell you that I have seen beings who–
iti70:3.2 | P: Diṭṭhā mayā, bhikkhave, sattā kāyaduccaritena samannāgatā vacīduccaritena samannāgatā manoduccaritena samannāgatā ariyānaṁ upavādakā micchādiṭṭhikā micchādiṭṭhikammasamādānā. | T: endowed with bodily misconduct, verbal misconduct, & mental misconduct; who reviled noble ones, held wrong views and undertook actions under the influence of wrong views–
iti70:3.3 | P: Te kāyassa bhedā paraṁ maraṇā apāyaṁ duggatiṁ vinipātaṁ nirayaṁ upapannā. | T: at the break-up of the body, after death, have re-appeared in a plane of deprivation, a bad destination, a lower realm, hell.
iti70:3.4 | S: I only say it because I’ve known, seen, and realized it for myself.” | T: It is from having known it myself, seen it myself, realized it myself that I tell you that I have seen beings who–
iti70:4.1 | P: Diṭṭhā mayā, bhikkhave, sattā kāyaduccaritena samannāgatā vacīduccaritena samannāgatā manoduccaritena samannāgatā ariyānaṁ upavādakā micchādiṭṭhikā micchādiṭṭhikammasamādānā. | T: endowed with bodily misconduct, verbal misconduct, & mental misconduct; who reviled noble ones, held wrong views and undertook actions under the influence of wrong views–
iti70:4.2 | P: Te kāyassa bhedā paraṁ maraṇā apāyaṁ duggatiṁ vinipātaṁ nirayaṁ upapannā”ti. | T: at the break-up of the body, after death, have re-appeared in a plane of deprivation, a bad destination, a lower realm, hell.”
iti70:4.3 | S: The Buddha spoke this matter. | T: (none)
iti70:4.4 | S: On this it is said: | T: (none)
iti70:5.1 | S: “When the mind has been misdirected, | T: With mind wrongly directed,
iti70:5.2 | S: and words wrongly spoken, | T: speaking wrong speech,
iti70:5.3 | S: and wrong bodily deeds have been done, | T: doing wrong deeds with the body:
iti70:5.4 | S: an individual here | T: a person here
iti70:6.1 | S: unlearned, doer of bad deeds, | T: of next-to-nothing learning, a doer of evil
iti70:6.2 | S: though their life may be short, | T: here in this next-to-nothing life,
iti70:6.3 | S: when their body breaks up, that witless person | T: at the break-up of the body, undiscerning,
iti70:6.4 | S: is reborn in hell.” | T: reappears in hell.
iti70:7.1 | S: This too is a matter that was spoken by the Blessed One: that is what I heard. | T: (none)
iti70:7.2 | P: Paṭhamaṁ. | T: (none)


